    "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204115": {
      "title": "Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training",
      "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Graduate Department of Psychology and Counseling Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Aug 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part Time Non Exempt Position ID: 204115 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.  Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: We are seeking a detail oriented and professional Assistant to the Director of Clinical Training (DCT) within a doctoral psychology training program. This position involves assisting with the internship application process for doctoral students pursuing APA accredited internships and supporting various administrative and educational initiatives related to clinical training. The position is 20 hours per week, from September 1 to June 1, with flexible hours except during scheduled in person fall workshops. Responsibilities: Reviewing and proofreading internship application materials, including CVs, cover letters, essays, and supplemental documents for clarity, formatting, grammar, and professionalism. Assists with organizing and coordinating internship preparation activities, such as interview workshops, mock interviews, informational meetings, and application timelines. Tracking student application progress, maintaining organizational systems and spreadsheets, communicating with students regarding deadlines and materials, and assisting with scheduling related activities and events. The individual in this role will develop familiarity with APPIC, APA internship standards, and the doctoral internship application process. Ideal candidates are organized, dependable, proactive, and interested in graduate training, psychology, higher education, or academic administration. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree required; background in psychology, education, counseling, English, communications, or a related field preferred Strong written communication, proofreading, and editing skills Excellent attention to detail and organizational abilities Ability to manage multiple deadlines and tasks simultaneously in a fast paced environment Professional interpersonal and communication skills, particularly when working with doctoral level students, faculty, and training sites Ability to provide constructive feedback in a supportive and professional manner Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and general administrative technology platforms Ability to maintain strict confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive student, academic, and training related information Understanding of professional boundaries, discretion, and ethical conduct within an academic and clinical training environment Preferred Requirements: Prior administrative or academic support experience Experience reviewing professional or academic writing materials Familiarity with graduate education, psychology training, or internship application processes Experience coordinating workshops, events, or student programming Strong formatting skills for professional documents and application materials Previous experience with editing, administrative support, student support services, or psychology related settings is preferred Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"
    },
    "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=161063": {
      "title": "Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct",
      "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Adjunct  - MBA Program Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct  - MBA Program Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct  - MBA Program Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business Locations: Malvern, PA, PA Posted: Apr 11, 2023 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Position ID: 161063 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Job Description: Immaculata University invites applications for adjunct business faculty positions for our new Master's of Business Administration (MBA) program . Candidates interested in developing course material and implementing innovative educational strategies to a diverse student population are encouraged to apply. Courses will be run in an online synchronous format over a 7- week period. Classes to be staffed include: Quantitative Decision Making Financial Analysis for Leaders People and Organizations Emerging Topics in Business Contemporary Marketing Avoiding Organizational Failure Financial Planning The successful candidate will: Create and manage syllabi for courses taught Create lesson plans and execute online synchronous lessons Meet with students during scheduled class meeting times Assess student learning based on quantitative assessment tools Provide students with feedback on assignments in a timely manner Respond to students' questions, and be available to assist students in learning course materials Promote the mission of the business department and Immaculata University Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: The ideal candidate will have an earned MBA, teaching experience at the college level, and industry experience in the appropriate field. Preference will be given to candidates with an earned doctorate in a relevant field. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Copies of transcripts of  undergraduate and graduate degrees (to be provided upon hire) Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"
