sdays; 11:00 - 12:15 PM) FIN 306 Money and Banking (Mondays & Wednesdays; 12:30 - 1:45 PM) Candidates interested in working with a team to implement innovative educational strategies to a diverse student population are encouraged to apply. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach in-person on the assigned day and time. Provide quality and timely feedback to students Assist in all retention efforts for business students; Ensure adherence to best practices and industry standards Increase awareness among students of the various resources available on campus to ensure academic and personal success and to direct them appropriately; Demonstrate a commitment to all forms of diversity; Be an advocate of and support the University's mission, vision, values and goals; Perform additional duties as assigned by the Chair and Dean. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in Finance, Financial Planning, Economics, Business Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Three (3) or more years of professional experience in finance, banking, wealth management, financial planning, insurance, risk management, investments, or a related field. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work effectively with diverse student populations. Preferred Requirements: One or more relevant professional designations such as CFP, CFA, ChFC, CPA/PFS, CIMA, RICP, CLU, or equivalent. Prior college-level teaching experience, preferably in face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online formats. Experience in financial planning, wealth management, investment management, banking, insurance, estate planning, or related fields. Experience teaching in a CFP Board Registered Program or familiarity with CFP certification requirements. Doctoral degree in Finance, Business, Economics, or a related discipline. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"
