      "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Nursing Clinical Coordinator - Division of Nursing Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Clinical Coordinator - Division of Nursing Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nursing Clinical Coordinator - Division of Nursing Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing - 4 year Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Jul 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Exempt Position ID: 202667 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Generous paid time off benefits. Tuition Assistance: You, your spouse, and your eligible dependent children can receive tuition assistance at IU.  Your dependent children are also eligible for tuition assistance at other institutions via the Tuition Exchange program. Health. Life, and Disability Insurance: Prescription, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance; Disability benefits, Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account. Retirement Plan: Generous retirement plan to help you save for your future. Job Description: Immaculata University invites applications for a full-time Nursing Clinical Coordinator. This role is responsible for the comprehensive coordination, organization, and oversight of undergraduate nursing student clinical and lab rotations and the procurement of necessary instructional faculty. The Coordinator serves as a vital liaison among the nursing program, healthcare partners, and regulatory bodies to ensure all clinical learning environments and faculty staffing meet program outcomes and Pennsylvania Board of Nursing (PA BON) requirements. The Clinical Coordinator collaborates with program leadership and clinical partners to facilitate student placements, maintain clinical affiliation requirements, and support the effective delivery of clinical education experiences. Responsibilities: Coordinate undergraduate nursing student clinical and lab placements across affiliated healthcare agencies and clinical practice settings. Maintain clinical rotation schedules, placement records, and student assignment information. Collaborate with healthcare agencies to secure and confirm clinical placements that align with course and program objectives. Coordinate onboarding requirements for clinical placements including orientation schedules, agency-specific requirements, and access procedures. Assist in balancing student placements to ensure appropriate clinical capacity and learning opportunities. Serve as a primary contact between the nursing program and affiliated clinical agencies. Maintain positive working relationships with clinical partners, nurse managers, educators, and preceptors. Communicate program expectations, schedules, and placement needs to clinical agencies in a timely manner. Participate in meetings with healthcare partners regarding clinical education operations and partnership development. Assist with maintaining and monitoring clinical affiliation agreements, as directed. Collaborate with course faculty and program leadership regarding clinical scheduling, placement needs, and site-specific requirements. Assist students with clinical onboarding processes and provide guidance related to clinical placement expectations. Communicate clinical schedules, assignments, and updates to students and faculty. Address and escalate clinical placement concerns or scheduling conflicts, as appropriate. Support orientation activities for students entering clinical settings. Verify with the compliance coordinator that students assigned to clinical rotations meet institutional, agency, and PA Board of Nursing clinical compliance requirements prior to placement. Maintain accurate records related to clinical placements, agency requirements, and student assignments. Assist with preparation of reports and documentation for accreditation reviews, audits, and program evaluation activities. Ensure adherence to policies and standards established by clinical agencies, regulatory bodies, and accrediting organizations Assist with evaluating clinical site utilization and identifying opportunities for expanded partnerships. Support continuous improvement initiatives related to clinical education operations and processes. Perform additional duties related to clinical education coordination as assigned. Provides clinical site educators and students with materials, including division of nursing policies, information or clinical site orientation, address, contact person, phone numbers, and parking information Responsible for onboarding procedure for newly hired adjunct faculty Communicates with business office concerning certificates of insurance and affiliation agreements. Participate in Division of Nursing and campus events to support institutional goals and community engagement. Collaborate with the Division of Nursing (DON) Chair and the Assistant Director of Lab/Clinical to conduct regular site visits to evaluate the quality of clinical environments. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Division Chair and Dean. Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) required. Current unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Minimum of 2 years of clinical nursing experience. Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and database or scheduling systems. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, and healthcare partners. Preferred Requirements: MSN in Nursing preferred, or willingness to obtain. Experience in nursing education, clinical instruction, or student placement coordination. Knowledge of undergraduate nursing clinical education requirements and accreditation standards. Experience working with healthcare systems and clinical affiliation processes. Familiarity with clinical scheduling or placement software systems. Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"
    },
    "https://immaculata.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204120": {
      "title": "Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time",
      "description": "Immaculata University\nJob Posting: Part-Time - Head Coach Men's Tennis Immaculata University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time - Head Coach Men's Tennis Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time - Head Coach Men's Tennis Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Malvern, PA Posted: Aug 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Ref. No.: Original Req: 347550 Position ID: 204120 Share About Immaculata University: Immaculata University seeks candidates who are passionate about upholding the value of higher education while fostering institutional excellence. Immaculata University is a comprehensive, co-ed institution of higher learning that has emphasized academic success, student outcomes and faith-based values for more than 100 years. Offering more than 75 in-demand undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs, Immaculata University provides attainable education, personal support and meaningful career pathways to tomorrow's leaders who are focused on intellectual, personal, professional and spiritual growth. Immaculata's expansive suburban campus is located in renowned Chester County, Pennsylvania, 30 miles west of Philadelphia. Why Immaculata University is the Perfect Workplace for you: Collegial Atmosphere, caring leadership, work/life balance. Mission-driven values supported by five core values: faith, community, knowledge, virtue and service. Job Description: The Head Coach leads and maintains an effective Division III sports program through recruiting, on-court/field teaching techniques, scheduling and maintaining a competitive conference season, maintain NCAA standards, budget management, fundraising, as well as promoting the sport throughout the University and local community. The Head Coach is responsible for all aspect that relate to the sports program including the ongoing development of the student athlete, promoting their physical, academic, and social growth in line with the mission and values of the University.  The Head Coach is expected to serve as the public face of the program, creating and maintaining a positive public image while recruiting and training student-athletes to compete at the highest level possible. This position reports to the Athletics Director. Responsibilities: Develop and implement a comprehensive training program to enhance players' skills, knowledge, and performance in tennis. Plan and conduct regular practices, focusing on individual and team development, strategy implementation, and game preparation Provide instruction and guidance to players on proper techniques, rules, and strategies specific to collegiate tennis Teach and set expectations of appropriate team conduct during competition, travel, practice and at all University events, and at any other times when the team is representing the University. Evaluate players' abilities and provide constructive feedback to help them improve their skills and performance. Develop game plans and strategies to maximize the team's chances of success during competitions Ensure compliance with Atlantic East Conference and university policies and procedures. Meet student athlete recruiting goals as established by the Director of Athletics and Recreation Achieve and maintain certification for CPR/AED and First Aid Monitor team fundraising account and ensure accurate coordination and reporting of funds usage and maintenance in accordance with university guidelines Develop and maintain alumni relations for the promotion of the program. Represent the University and its athletics program, with honesty, integrity, and sportsmanship at all times, to various institutional programs and students, parents and families, the general public, alumni and external agencies. Work with various departments and personnel at the university to aid in the development of a positive student-athlete experience. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics and Recreation Immaculata University is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree with successful collegiate or high school tennis coaching experience Additional Information: Special Requirements Background check required after a conditional job offer is made. Consideration of the background check will be tailored to the requirements of the job. MVR check is required for this role. Application Instructions: Required Documents: Resume Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Immaculata University 1145 KING ROAD IMMACULATA, PA. 19345"
